\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Glory to Thee, my God, this night,
\par For all the blessings of the light:
\par Keep me, O keep me, King of kings;
\par Beneath Thine own almighty wings.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Forgive me, Lord, for Thy dear Son,
\par The ill that I this day have done;
\par That with the world, myself, and Thee,
\par I, ere I sleep, at peace may be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Teach me to live, that I may dread
\par The grave as little as my bed;
\par Teach me to die, that so I may
\par Rise glorious at the awful day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O may my soul on Thee repose,
\par And may sweet sleep mine eyelids close;
\par Sleep that may me more vigorous make
\par To serve my God when I awake.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. If in  the night I sleepless lie,
\par My soul with heavenly thoughts supply;
\par Let no ill dreams disturb my rest,
\par No powers of darkness me molest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O may I always ready stand
\par With my lamp  burning in my hand;
\par May I in sight of heaven rejoice,
\par Whene'er I hear the Bridegroom's voice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. All praise to Thee in light arrayed,
\par Who light Thy dwelling- place hast made;
\par A boundless ocean of bright beams
\par From Thy all- glorious Godhead streams.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Praise God, from whom all blessings flow,
\par Praise Him, all creatures here below;
\par Praise Him above, ye heavenly host:
\par Praise Father, Son and Holy Ghost.
\par                                        Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

